WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.975
These two conditions look similar but they represent
different policies Without parentheses

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:09.950
AND is evaluated first so the consent requirement
applies only to the

00:00:09.962 --> 00:00:15.138
Kidney Disease branch Any patient age sixty-five or
older can qualify even

00:00:15.162 --> 00:00:20.350
when consent is false With parentheses the age and
diagnosis alternatives are

00:00:20.375 --> 00:00:25.250
grouped together and explicit consent is required
for the entire rule Run

00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:29.788
both statements and compare the rows Lisa Ray is the
useful boundary

00:00:29.812 --> 00:00:34.675
record age seventy-one but consent is false She
appears only in the

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:39.600
unparenthesized version This is why parentheses are
part of the meaning not

00:00:39.612 --> 00:00:40.425
just formatting
